<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle by Tauri. One key, and it is here rather than in Rust because a usage
  description is not a platform *seam* — `src-tauri/tests/platform_seams.rs` caps `#[cfg(target_os)]`
  at two files, and this costs nothing against that budget.

  macOS attributes a child process's microphone access to the responsible application, so this is
  what produces the prompt when SoX runs. Claude Code ships a whole helper .app for the same reason:
  a bare CLI binary has no bundle to put this in. wtm already is one.

  A signed release needs one more thing: the hardened runtime denies the microphone without even
  this prompt unless the app also carries `com.apple.security.device.audio-input`, which
  Entitlements.plist supplies.

  Known rough edge, documented in the README rather than hidden: a local build is signed ad-hoc, so
  its TCC grant is keyed to a signature that changes on every rebuild — the prompt comes back after
  `just build`. A release's Developer ID signature does not change, so its grant survives updates.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>wtm records your voice only while you hold the dictation button in a prompt composer, and sends that recording to Deepgram to be turned into text.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
